{"name":"Livid","hex":"#6688cc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"livid","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a dark, bluish appearance.","Pale, pallid."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/livid"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blue-gray","blocks":[{"text":"Blue-gray is a medium blue-gray color on the cool side of the color wheel. The name blue-gray was introduced by Crayola for a crayon color used from 1958 to 1990. The complementary color is #CC9966, a warm khaki or brown."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blue-gray","wikidata":"Q4928721"},{"title":"Livid (festival)","blocks":[{"text":"Livid was an Australian alternative rock music festival held annually from 1989 to 2003. Created by Peter Walsh and Natalie Jeremijenko, the original idea of showcasing both the arts (Natalie) and music (Peter) in the one event was standardised as late as October/early November from 1991 until 2003. While it has never been officially cancelled, no festivals have been held since 2003 and neither the organisers nor promoters have announced any intention to restart Livid in the future."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livid_(festival)","wikidata":"Q6658883"},{"title":"Livid (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Livid is a 2011 French supernatural horror film written and directed by Julien Maury and Alexandre Bustillo. It is their follow-up to the horror film Inside."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/b/b8/Livid_Poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Livid_(film)","wikidata":"Q3257139"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Glacial_iceberg_in_Argentina.jpg/500px-Glacial_iceberg_in_Argentina.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/03/Glacial_iceberg_in_Argentina.jpg/1280px-Glacial_iceberg_in_Argentina